WEBVTT

01:31.508 --> 01:36.471
SECOND STORY
FIRST PERFORMANCE

01:41.476 --> 01:44.103
What the hell am I doing?

01:44.187 --> 01:46.314
A Rakugoka who's on his way up.

01:46.397 --> 01:48.066
Which is me, Guriko Arakawa.

01:48.650 --> 01:51.027
Tailing my own master like this...

01:52.529 --> 01:54.030
Forgive me, Master.

01:54.114 --> 01:56.324
It's all because of what happened
on set yesterday.

01:56.407 --> 01:59.285
Could you teach me everything
you know about fishing?

01:59.369 --> 02:01.496
Who cares about that stuff?

02:01.579 --> 02:03.998
Just tell me the secret behind it!

02:07.669 --> 02:08.962
Guriko, got a second?

02:09.045 --> 02:11.506
Hey, Riichi. What's up?

02:11.589 --> 02:14.300
You trained under Master Shiguma, right?

02:14.384 --> 02:15.552
Right!

02:15.635 --> 02:19.139
Shiguma Arakawa's last apprentice
is yours truly!

02:19.931 --> 02:22.016
I don't know how to tell you this, but...

02:22.725 --> 02:25.895
All this talk about Master Shiguma
dating a young girl...

02:25.979 --> 02:28.481
- Is that true?
- Huh? What's up with that?

02:29.190 --> 02:33.194
There's a bunch of people
who've seen them walking side by side.

02:35.738 --> 02:37.240
It's true.

02:37.323 --> 02:39.075
Said no one ever!

02:42.912 --> 02:43.746
He went inside!

02:44.747 --> 02:46.583
Karaoke?

02:49.961 --> 02:51.170
In there, huh?

02:58.303 --> 03:01.180
Wait. No way.

03:02.390 --> 03:04.392
So it's true!

03:07.145 --> 03:09.522
Huh? What are those two doing?

03:09.606 --> 03:11.983
Rakugo? Is it that kind of game?

03:12.483 --> 03:13.735
But the master's face...

03:14.777 --> 03:16.446
couldn't be more serious!

03:17.113 --> 03:19.324
Excuse me, sir?

03:19.407 --> 03:21.576
- Is there a problem?
- Huh?

03:22.160 --> 03:25.038
Oh, uh... No, no, nothing at all.

03:28.291 --> 03:31.502
Sir!

03:36.090 --> 03:37.592
You damned fool!

03:38.176 --> 03:41.554
You heard a baseless rumor and
took it upon yourself to tail me?

03:42.138 --> 03:44.015
How could you be so ridiculous?

03:44.515 --> 03:45.391
Shame on you!

03:46.809 --> 03:49.562
Well, if you hadn't been so sneaky...

03:51.272 --> 03:52.649
you wouldn't have blown it, right?

03:53.650 --> 03:55.777
Hey! Do you know who
you're talking to? You cheeky...

03:56.361 --> 03:58.988
Master, who is this little twerp?

03:59.072 --> 04:02.992
She's Akane Osaki, Shinta's daughter.

04:04.369 --> 04:05.662
Nice to meet ya!

04:07.413 --> 04:08.998
Th-This kid?

04:10.083 --> 04:13.461
The daughter of Shinta Ani-san,
who got expelled six years ago?

04:14.337 --> 04:15.838
Never mind that.

04:18.424 --> 04:21.177
How was my Rakugo?

04:22.303 --> 04:25.765
Ever since that day, six years ago
since you started training me...

04:26.557 --> 04:29.644
I still don't have permission to perform
Rakugo in front of an audience.

04:30.144 --> 04:33.731
But I'm going to be 17 this year,
and I'm a senior in high school.

04:34.816 --> 04:37.568
- So you haven't changed your mind?
- No.

04:39.696 --> 04:41.781
I'm going to become a Shin'uchi
of the Arakawa School.

04:43.157 --> 04:47.787
I'll become a Shin'uchi, and show them
how amazing Dad's art was.

04:47.870 --> 04:48.913
Everyone...

04:49.414 --> 04:50.665
That man...

04:52.292 --> 04:54.168
I'm going to prove it!

04:54.919 --> 04:56.671
Please allow me to train under you!

04:58.464 --> 05:01.467
Time sure does fly, doesn't it?

05:08.057 --> 05:10.435
Make you my apprentice?

05:10.518 --> 05:14.147
But Akane, you're still in grade school.

05:15.315 --> 05:17.608
Why do you want to become a Rakugoka?

05:19.152 --> 05:21.696
What on earth happened?

05:26.326 --> 05:30.288
Dad started working for a company
that sells concrete.

05:31.914 --> 05:34.792
He said he couldn't just
keep brooding all the time,

05:34.876 --> 05:37.253
so he started working.

05:37.336 --> 05:39.797
- All right, I'll head over now.
- He seems so busy every day.

05:41.299 --> 05:42.717
But because of that,

05:43.718 --> 05:46.304
he now earns more money
than he ever earned from Rakugo.

05:46.387 --> 05:49.640
We can even go out to eat dinner.

05:52.643 --> 05:55.521
Isn't that a good thing, though?

05:56.647 --> 05:58.691
That's what everyone says.

05:58.775 --> 05:59.901
That it's a good thing.

06:01.360 --> 06:04.864
A good thing that Dad quit Rakugo...

06:05.364 --> 06:07.617
That he was forced to quit Rakugo...

06:08.618 --> 06:11.412
But I really loved Dad's Rakugo!

06:11.496 --> 06:13.289
Even though he was the only one talking,

06:13.372 --> 06:16.834
I could see all kinds of people
and scenery, like magic.

06:18.169 --> 06:22.298
That's why it makes me sad to think that
I'll never see Dad's Rakugo again.

06:23.341 --> 06:27.345
But when Dad quit Rakugo,

06:27.428 --> 06:31.390
everyone said, "He's serious now,"
and they all smile and laugh.

06:33.101 --> 06:35.603
The only one who was sad was me.

06:36.354 --> 06:38.856
Every time someone said,
"Aren't you glad?"

06:38.940 --> 06:42.777
it felt like they were saying
Dad's Rakugo was no good.

06:42.860 --> 06:43.986
It made me so bitter.

06:45.321 --> 06:46.781
So I made up my mind!

06:46.864 --> 06:51.285
I'm going to become a Shin'uchi,
and prove that Dad's Rakugo was great!

06:59.710 --> 07:02.880
You've grown. Truly.

07:04.882 --> 07:06.676
Apprenticeship with just
a high school degree...

07:06.759 --> 07:10.138
That's rare nowadays,
but not completely unheard of.

07:10.763 --> 07:12.974
If there is a problem at all...

07:13.057 --> 07:14.600
It's with me.

07:15.476 --> 07:17.937
I'm not fit to take on an apprentice.

07:18.020 --> 07:19.939
But still...

07:22.150 --> 07:23.443
Sorry, Akane.

07:24.444 --> 07:25.611
Hello?

07:25.695 --> 07:28.322
Oh, it's been a long time!

07:28.406 --> 07:29.282
What?

07:29.782 --> 07:31.951
Well, that sounds like trouble!

07:32.034 --> 07:33.953
Let me find someone for you.

07:34.036 --> 07:35.329
All right, I'll talk to you later.

07:36.372 --> 07:38.416
Master, is something the matter?

07:38.499 --> 07:40.918
That was Ms. Yoshino from the Rakugo Cafe.

07:41.002 --> 07:44.255
She's looking for someone
to perform today.

07:44.338 --> 07:45.423
That's short notice.

07:45.506 --> 07:48.968
Seems like her solo performer
is running late.

07:49.051 --> 07:50.094
Is that right?

07:50.803 --> 07:52.972
Understood! Then I'll...

07:53.055 --> 07:55.641
Yes. Akane, you go.

07:55.725 --> 07:57.310
- Huh? You sure?
- What?

07:57.977 --> 08:03.357
Akane, becoming my apprentice literally
means becoming a professional Rakugoka.

08:03.441 --> 08:06.027
Now go get a look at the world of pros!

08:07.153 --> 08:08.654
Understood.

08:09.155 --> 08:12.074
I'll bring the house down with laughter,
and leave them speechless!

08:12.158 --> 08:14.076
Just wait and see!

08:15.077 --> 08:16.037
RAKUGO CAFE

08:16.120 --> 08:17.205
Oh, it's you, Guri-chan!

08:17.788 --> 08:19.165
Thank you for filling in today.

08:19.248 --> 08:23.836
Uh, no, I'm not the one
going on stage today.

08:26.214 --> 08:27.048
It's her.

08:27.131 --> 08:29.425
What? This girl?

08:30.051 --> 08:32.345
Oh, are you Ms. Yoshino?

08:32.428 --> 08:33.930
What? Uh, yes.

08:34.013 --> 08:38.184
I've been entrusted with the role of
substitute performer by Shiguma Arakawa.

08:38.267 --> 08:40.269
My name is Akane Osaki!

08:40.353 --> 08:44.815
I will devote myself wholeheartedly
to this once-in-a-lifetime opportunity!

08:44.899 --> 08:46.526
Thank you for your support!

08:46.609 --> 08:48.694
Who is this girl?

08:49.820 --> 08:51.864
What a sweet child she is!

08:51.948 --> 08:54.325
And thank you for your support!

08:54.408 --> 08:55.743
AKANE

08:55.826 --> 08:57.328
Who's Akane?

08:57.411 --> 08:59.956
That's unusual, using just her first name.

09:00.039 --> 09:02.083
I wonder which school she's from?

09:04.460 --> 09:06.170
What? Not an apprentice?

09:06.254 --> 09:07.630
And it's her first performance, no less?

09:08.214 --> 09:09.632
If it gets bad, I'll clean up after her!

09:09.715 --> 09:10.883
So please let her perform.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.344
Guri-chan really implored me.

09:16.138 --> 09:18.975
When the music starts, you're up, okay?

09:20.643 --> 09:22.645
- Did you hear me?
- What?

09:22.728 --> 09:25.398
Oh, uh... Hey, you're right!

09:25.481 --> 09:28.526
This kimono that I borrowed
from Master fits me like a glove!

09:28.609 --> 09:30.820
You've got butterflies, huh?

09:30.903 --> 09:33.239
What? Huh? No, I do not!

09:33.322 --> 09:35.575
Well, listen up. Ready?

09:35.658 --> 09:38.452
You write "people" on your
dominant hand and swallow it.

09:39.036 --> 09:40.746
Dominant hand signifies the audience.

09:41.998 --> 09:45.293
A Rakugoka dominates the audience, see?

09:46.043 --> 09:48.296
The master's been known
to do it too, for major shows.

09:48.379 --> 09:49.630
The master does it?

09:52.300 --> 09:55.052
- So you are nervous after all!
- Shut up!

09:56.470 --> 09:58.055
Well, don't get too worked up.

10:01.058 --> 10:03.436
Hey, are you actually a nice guy?

10:03.519 --> 10:05.187
What do mean, actually?

10:05.271 --> 10:06.856
Sorry! I didn't mean that.

10:08.941 --> 10:10.151
Thank you.

10:13.487 --> 10:15.156
I feel a little more relaxed now.

10:22.246 --> 10:23.122
All right.

10:26.000 --> 10:27.084
I'm heading out now.

10:34.925 --> 10:35.760
AKANE

10:44.435 --> 10:46.145
Whoa. A crowd!

10:46.646 --> 10:48.606
Well, not that I didn't know.

10:49.231 --> 10:50.566
I knew there would be.

10:55.571 --> 10:56.489
But seeing it from here...

10:59.200 --> 11:00.409
The pressure's crazy!

11:02.453 --> 11:05.081
And somehow, I totally feel...

11:06.374 --> 11:07.541
all alone.

11:09.126 --> 11:12.755
But I made the decision myself
to come here.

11:17.301 --> 11:18.761
Don't fold.

11:18.844 --> 11:20.179
Don't run away.

11:20.888 --> 11:22.264
Let it all out!

11:23.015 --> 11:24.725
Everything you've been building until now...

11:27.895 --> 11:30.523
What exists inside me...

11:31.941 --> 11:32.983
Today, right here...

11:33.818 --> 11:34.777
All of it!

11:35.861 --> 11:39.782
Uh, we all have our likes and dislikes.

11:39.865 --> 11:42.326
Thank goodness, she started talking!

11:42.410 --> 11:45.579
Her voice is strong,
and her gestures are bold.

11:48.374 --> 11:50.918
Hey, what a shock! Man, what a shock!

11:51.001 --> 11:53.129
Rakugo is a dialogue-based play.

11:53.212 --> 11:55.881
You portray each character by yourself
and through their exchanges,

11:55.965 --> 11:57.591
you mine the audience for laughs.

11:57.675 --> 12:00.469
It was slithering, with jaws opening wide...

12:00.553 --> 12:03.389
Its long tongue going, flicka-flick!
There was a snake, see?

12:03.472 --> 12:05.057
Man, was I shocked!

12:05.141 --> 12:06.725
Huh? For real?

12:06.809 --> 12:08.727
So what about you? What are you afraid of?

12:09.728 --> 12:10.980
"Scared of Manju."

12:11.063 --> 12:14.483
A story about young men talking
about what they're afraid of,

12:14.567 --> 12:16.110
and the ensuing commotion.

12:16.193 --> 12:19.947
A familiar Rakugo classic. But...

12:20.656 --> 12:22.616
There's something I'm scared of.
What did I tell you?

12:22.700 --> 12:25.536
Oh, dear me! What is this?

12:25.619 --> 12:30.499
This isn't something that a first timer
with no master can accomplish!

12:30.583 --> 12:31.417
Oh, come on.

12:34.503 --> 12:35.504
Manju.

12:37.047 --> 12:40.259
What was that? Huh? Manju?

12:40.342 --> 12:42.636
Say what? Hey, are there any bugs
called manju?

12:42.720 --> 12:45.598
But what is this? It feels so nostalgic.

12:45.681 --> 12:48.142
That guy says he's afraid of manju!

12:48.225 --> 12:52.062
Hey, seeing manju will kill him,
so wouldn't that be an AN-ssassination?

12:52.938 --> 12:53.772
Shin-chan!

13:00.112 --> 13:01.947
Manju!

13:02.031 --> 13:04.742
Hey! I told you how scared I am of manju,

13:04.825 --> 13:08.496
so you all bought some,
and you're trying to kill me!

13:09.371 --> 13:11.957
Manju... So scary!

13:12.041 --> 13:13.459
Manju...

13:13.542 --> 13:15.419
So scared... I'm so scared!

13:15.503 --> 13:17.379
Of manju...

13:17.463 --> 13:20.090
Oh, so scared... Of manju!

13:20.174 --> 13:23.010
I'm terrified! So scared...

13:23.844 --> 13:25.221
What's this? Hey...

13:26.430 --> 13:27.932
It's just crushed red bean paste manju?

13:36.232 --> 13:37.566
And what do we have here?

13:37.650 --> 13:40.653
A buckwheat manju, right? Isn't it?

13:40.736 --> 13:43.864
Oh, I'm so scared!
Come on, quit messing with me!

13:43.948 --> 13:48.118
Hey, where'd all those butterflies go?

13:48.202 --> 13:51.372
You're not even fazed
by your first performance.

13:51.455 --> 13:53.832
Damn it.
Like hell, you're "Scared of Manju."

13:55.167 --> 13:57.545
You're the scariest of all!

14:00.422 --> 14:01.882
Well, this sucks.

14:01.966 --> 14:06.136
At last my dream came true, and I got my
first solo performance at the Rakugo Cafe.

14:06.220 --> 14:11.850
But thanks to that accident, I got stuck
on that bus for three and a half hours.

14:11.934 --> 14:12.810
It's so not funny.

14:13.769 --> 14:16.188
I've really made the audience wait on me.

14:16.272 --> 14:17.898
I feel so bad.

14:30.119 --> 14:31.745
I'm scared of manju!

14:31.829 --> 14:34.206
How could you, Master Shiguma?

14:34.790 --> 14:37.501
Sending over a girl without telling me
a thing about her,

14:37.585 --> 14:39.420
then asking me what I think of her?

14:40.504 --> 14:44.341
What else can I possibly say but that
her performance was splendid?

14:44.425 --> 14:45.342
Listen, you jerk!

14:45.926 --> 14:49.221
You've been gobbling those manju while
screaming how scared you are of them.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.307
So what the hell are you really scared of?

14:51.390 --> 14:55.185
Oh, well. What I'm scared of now
is some bitter tea!

15:17.166 --> 15:18.083
Good job.

15:19.293 --> 15:20.419
Thanks.

15:21.337 --> 15:24.298
So how was your first-ever performance?

15:25.758 --> 15:26.842
More exhausting than I thought.

15:27.843 --> 15:30.012
Well, you did speak
for 20 minutes straight.

15:30.596 --> 15:33.390
Yeah, but I'll take this
kind of exhaustion any day!

15:38.979 --> 15:41.607
I wonder if they'll let me do it again?

15:41.690 --> 15:43.943
Don't get cocky, you dummy! You--

15:44.026 --> 15:47.780
Amazing!

15:50.532 --> 15:52.493
That was incredible! Incredible!

15:52.576 --> 15:54.662
Are you a teenager?
You're younger than me, right?

15:54.745 --> 15:55.829
Boy, that was stunning!

15:55.913 --> 15:58.832
You really made that boisterous
row house come alive!

15:58.916 --> 16:02.753
Your tone of voice and your tempo is like
Master Shiguma's, but a little different.

16:02.836 --> 16:04.171
Tell me, where do you usually perform?

16:04.254 --> 16:05.673
Hey! You...

16:05.756 --> 16:07.383
Well? Well? Well, well?

16:08.342 --> 16:10.803
I totally get why you did that.

16:10.886 --> 16:11.887
But that guy's up next.

16:11.971 --> 16:14.264
Huh? That's your concern? Who cares?

16:14.348 --> 16:15.808
Ouch, ouch.

16:15.891 --> 16:17.309
Hey, sorry.

16:17.393 --> 16:20.854
When I meet a talented Rakugoka,
I just can't hold myself back.

16:20.938 --> 16:23.357
But seriously, your
"Scared of Manju" was great!

16:23.440 --> 16:24.984
Especially how you gobbled those manju.

16:25.067 --> 16:27.778
You slightly changed how you ate
the chestnut and kudzu manju.

16:27.861 --> 16:29.613
I was like, "Nailed it!"

16:30.823 --> 16:32.825
All right. I'm up.

16:34.159 --> 16:35.536
Wait a second.

16:35.619 --> 16:39.331
Since you did take the stage
to fill in for me...

16:40.082 --> 16:44.044
Yeah! As a special favor, I'll let you
watch my solo performance for free!

16:47.131 --> 16:49.258
Watch and learn from the wings.

16:53.971 --> 16:56.765
So arrogant! I wouldn't watch him
for anything!

16:56.849 --> 16:58.058
Oh, where's the harm?

16:58.142 --> 16:59.601
Let's learn from the guy.

17:00.310 --> 17:03.397
Apprenticed two years ago.
Promoted to Futatsume at 19.

17:03.480 --> 17:05.357
He's the Rakugoka
that everyone's talking about.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.775
It won't hurt to watch him.

17:07.359 --> 17:10.487
It pisses me off to say it,
but that guy's Rakugo...

17:15.409 --> 17:16.326
It's sensual.

17:16.910 --> 17:21.331
Uh, I know I've kept you all waiting
today for a very long time.

17:21.415 --> 17:23.751
But you were certainly in luck!

17:23.834 --> 17:27.296
The girl before me
was not only pretty, but talented!

17:27.880 --> 17:29.798
I wonder who's been teaching her Rakugo?

17:29.882 --> 17:31.383
Really, she was amazing.

17:31.467 --> 17:35.137
Aside from Rakugo, I'm sure there are
all kinds of things you can learn.

17:35.220 --> 17:38.640
But completing your studies
is certainly no small feat.

17:38.724 --> 17:40.476
Hello! Old Master!

17:40.559 --> 17:41.643
Yes, yes.

17:41.727 --> 17:44.396
Hey, Hattsan. Is something the matter?

17:44.480 --> 17:46.148
Oh, thank goodness you're here.

17:46.231 --> 17:48.484
Uh, you see, I want to be a ladies' man!

17:48.567 --> 17:49.693
I wanna be a catch!

17:49.777 --> 17:51.028
How should I do that?

17:51.111 --> 17:54.198
You're putting me on the spot,
asking me a question like that.

17:56.575 --> 17:58.952
He's homely, and he has no money.

17:59.036 --> 18:01.246
It's a tale of such a man
taking singing lessons

18:01.330 --> 18:03.999
from a master
so he can become a ladies' man.

18:04.083 --> 18:05.709
An Ongyoku-banashi.

18:07.002 --> 18:09.338
Oh, then would you like to hear a ballad?

18:09.421 --> 18:11.465
A ballad? Sure, sounds good.

18:11.548 --> 18:13.050
Oh, is that right? All right, then.

18:13.634 --> 18:16.970
Well, there's a ballad
called "The Loose Hair," so...

18:17.054 --> 18:19.264
What? Loose hair?

18:19.348 --> 18:22.017
That's what happens a lot
with those express buses, right?

18:22.101 --> 18:24.103
No, that would be loose schedules.

18:24.978 --> 18:26.730
This Rakugoka was aboard one,
and got stuck...

18:26.814 --> 18:29.024
He's a totally different person now.

18:29.108 --> 18:30.776
He's so sensual.

18:30.859 --> 18:34.154
I can't believe he can play
such a seductive woman.

18:34.238 --> 18:36.990
All right, why don't I sing it
for you first?

18:37.074 --> 18:39.493
You listen, and try to learn it.

18:40.077 --> 18:41.578
Are you ready, sir?

18:47.334 --> 18:53.090
If I were...

18:53.173 --> 18:55.134
Wow, his singing's great!

18:56.260 --> 19:02.808
A bush warbler...

19:03.392 --> 19:06.979
In my master's garden...

19:07.062 --> 19:08.438
He can do this kind of thing, too?

19:08.522 --> 19:10.524
So, something like that.

19:10.607 --> 19:12.901
What? You mean I gotta do that?

19:12.985 --> 19:15.112
All right, are you ready, sir?

19:15.696 --> 19:17.781
Three, two...

19:17.865 --> 19:21.493
If I were

19:21.577 --> 19:25.080
A bush warbler!

19:28.584 --> 19:30.127
Don't forget to take breaths.

19:31.962 --> 19:33.589
He's so polished,
it pisses you off, right?

19:33.672 --> 19:36.341
The essence of his art is sensuality.

19:36.425 --> 19:39.303
Because he can play sensual roles,

19:39.386 --> 19:41.263
it plays up the words and actions
of his dimwitted roles,

19:41.847 --> 19:43.932
leading to waves of laughter.

19:44.558 --> 19:46.643
Who is that guy?

19:47.728 --> 19:49.396
Kaisei Arakawa.

19:49.479 --> 19:50.314
KAISEI ARAKAWA

19:50.397 --> 19:52.858
Since the Shin'uchi
Promotion Test six years ago,

19:52.941 --> 19:57.696
he's the only man that Issho Arakawa
promoted to Futatsume.

20:06.121 --> 20:08.916
All these reviews are about him.

20:09.708 --> 20:13.837
I thought I did pretty well
out there myself, but...

20:13.921 --> 20:15.339
Well, well...

20:15.422 --> 20:17.633
They've written some
pretty nice things about me.

20:18.884 --> 20:21.345
Don't be so shocked. You wound me.

20:21.428 --> 20:24.723
But you were reading them pretty ardently.

20:24.806 --> 20:26.642
Could it be that I was on your mind?

20:26.725 --> 20:28.060
Not a chance.

20:28.143 --> 20:33.190
Oh, by the way, Akane, are you
training under Master Shiguma?

20:33.273 --> 20:34.733
No, not yet.

20:34.816 --> 20:36.777
Is that right? Then...

20:37.361 --> 20:40.656
Akane, why don't you train
under my master, too?

20:40.739 --> 20:41.573
Nope.

20:41.657 --> 20:44.368
That was quick! I'm sad to hear that.

20:44.451 --> 20:46.703
I mean, I was
pretty serious about it, too.

20:47.579 --> 20:50.707
My master's currently
gathering young talent

20:50.791 --> 20:54.711
to shake up the current
seniority-based Rakugo world.

20:55.420 --> 20:57.631
He only evaluates your artistic skill.

20:58.548 --> 21:01.343
It's the ideal environment for us.

21:01.426 --> 21:03.136
You should join us there, too, Akane.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.306
I see. Then...

21:07.266 --> 21:09.351
I think I'll start training
under Master Shiguma!

21:10.519 --> 21:11.812
Thanks! See you!

21:12.604 --> 21:14.856
Huh? Wait, what's that supposed to mean?

21:16.066 --> 21:17.943
Well, you just said it yourself.

21:18.026 --> 21:19.653
That he'll evaluate you if you're skilled.

21:21.238 --> 21:22.406
Oh, right.

21:22.906 --> 21:24.741
Kaisei Arakawa, sir!

21:25.492 --> 21:28.996
I lost to you today, but I'm going
to catch up before you know it.

21:29.538 --> 21:31.123
So brace yourself, all right?

21:33.458 --> 21:35.502
Akane!

21:35.585 --> 21:37.004
Look, look, look!

21:37.087 --> 21:41.049
Just look at all these reviews about you!

21:41.133 --> 21:43.385
I went to copy them all at once,
and it took me a while.

21:43.468 --> 21:45.304
Huh? Akane?

21:45.387 --> 21:46.680
Hey, we're heading back now.

21:46.763 --> 21:48.265
H-Huh?

21:48.348 --> 21:50.434
She didn't leave already, did she?

21:50.517 --> 21:52.561
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

23:35.997 --> 23:37.833
NEXT EPISODE
ELDER FELLOW APPRENTICE

23:38.708 --> 23:40.836
Akane Small Talk!

23:45.048 --> 23:47.342
My first performance sure was fun!

23:47.425 --> 23:49.219
Well, I guess it wasn't bad, huh?

23:49.302 --> 23:50.512
Before you start your apprenticeship,

23:50.595 --> 23:52.639
you should listen to a bunch
of Rakugokas and learn from them.

23:52.722 --> 23:53.807
Sure thing!

23:53.890 --> 23:54.933
Hey, I know.

23:55.016 --> 23:58.687
As your senpai, I'll tell you
where you should listen to Rakugo!

23:58.770 --> 24:00.355
Oh, that's okay. I already know.

24:00.438 --> 24:02.232
Don't be shy!

24:02.315 --> 24:03.650
First of all, yose.

24:03.733 --> 24:06.653
These are theaters made especially
to show the audience our art.

24:06.736 --> 24:08.864
The yose known as joseki
usually have performances

24:08.947 --> 24:14.077
365 days a year, from noon till night.

24:14.161 --> 24:15.162
Aside from Rakugo,

24:15.245 --> 24:19.457
they also feature a wide range of arts
like kodan, manzai, and kamikiri.

24:19.541 --> 24:22.377
If there are available seats,
you can just drop by that day,

24:22.460 --> 24:24.004
and you're free to come and go throughout!

24:24.087 --> 24:25.005
Awesome, huh?

24:25.088 --> 24:26.339
I told you, I already know that.

24:26.423 --> 24:31.928
Also, the more popular Rakugoka
do solo performances in bigger venues.

24:32.012 --> 24:34.639
If you want to immerse yourself
in your favorite Rakugoka's storytelling,

24:34.723 --> 24:35.765
I'd definitely recommend it!

24:35.849 --> 24:37.934
Hey, I need to tell Master about today.

24:38.018 --> 24:40.312
You can also watch Rakugo performances

24:40.395 --> 24:44.107
at community centers,
cafés, and even temples.

24:44.191 --> 24:47.319
Yeah, you really need
to keep an eye out for them.

24:47.861 --> 24:50.822
Huh? Hey!
